compile
@unchecked
Admits a fixed-width state-machine program from state and 16-bit word-slot counts, an initial state, bounded emit capacity, and transition rows. An optional sixth argument declares a separate bank of 18-bit address scratch slots; it does not widen ordinary word slots.

compile(state_count, slot_count, initial_state, emit_capacity, transitions, ...args)
===
new
@unchecked
Creates a mutable machine instance from an admitted program and initial 16-bit slot values. Optional bindings are typed word stores available to admitted load/store operations.

new(program, initial_slots, ...args)
===
step
@unchecked
Executes one admitted transition for event.

step(m, event)
===
run
@unchecked
Executes count repeated events through the admitted state-machine realization.

run(m, event, count)
===
run_until
@unchecked
Executes up to count repeated events and stops early when stop_state is reached.

run_until(m, event, count, stop_state)
===
state
@unchecked
Returns the current numeric state id.

state(m)
===
slot
@unchecked
Returns slot i as an Aiki number.

slot(m, i)
===
outputs
@unchecked
Returns the bounded observed output snapshot as [code, value] pairs.

outputs(m)
===
dropped
@unchecked
Returns the number of outputs dropped because the bounded output ring was full or disabled.

dropped(m)
===
staged_writes
@unchecked
Returns the number of transactional bound-store writes staged inside the machine and not yet committed.

staged_writes(m)
===
commit_writes
@unchecked
Applies the machine-local transactional write journal to its bound word stores in architectural order, then clears the journal. Staged writes are range-checked before commit and loads observe the staged overlay before commit.

commit_writes(m)
===
discard_writes
@unchecked
Clears the machine-local transactional write journal without modifying any bound word store.

discard_writes(m)
